.TH LIANLI-GUI 1 "" "Lian Li Linux"
.SH NAME
lianli-gui \- configure Lian Li hardware through the daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lianli-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
The desktop client configures supported fans, lighting and LCDs through daemon
IPC. Installation Health reports missing prerequisites and links focused repair
guides. Service controls select one user or system hardware daemon.
.PP
LCD and template edits use the GUI's Save/apply workflow. A saved setting does
not by itself confirm successful media preparation or physical display output;
inspect the reported runtime status when troubleshooting.
.PP
Hardware video acceleration defaults to disabled and is configured through GUI
settings. The daemon applies policy changes to affected streams at runtime.
.PP
The GUI offers managed media copies, asset-access checks and backup operations.
System-daemon access is checked separately from desktop-user access. Original
assets are retained when copying into managed storage.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Use Installation Health to recheck prerequisites. Diagnostic export includes
daemon logs; review the export before sharing it. A service manager is needed
for service actions, but standalone inspection is available through
.BR lianli-control (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lianli-daemon (1),
.BR lianli-control (1),
.BR lianli-session (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sgtaziz/lian-li-linux/tree/main/docs
